<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's YPF to place $100 million in bonds.</title>
<headline>Argentina's YPF to place $100 million in bonds.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine oil company YPF said Thursday it will issue $100 million in bonds guaranteed by export credits at a price of 99.768 for a yield of seven percent.</p>
<p>YPF said in a statement to the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange the issue will be placed on April 8 and will mature on October 26, 2002.</p>
<p>This bond is part of the oil company's negotiable bond program of $500 million approved last year.</p>
<p>((-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668))</p>
